    "seconds": 1.68,
    "verdict": "PARTIAL",
    "answer": "In quantization, the zero point refers to the value that represents the minimum input or output level for a quantized tensor. In symmetric quantization, both weights and activations are centered around zero, so the zero point is naturally zero. For asymmetric quantization, the zero point is chosen to align the quantized range with the data distribution."
